{
  "id": "29598_okoridasu",
  "headword": "{怒|おこ}り{出|だ}す",
  "reading": "おこりだす",
  "romaji": "okoridasu",
  "part_of_speech": "verb-godan",
  "gloss": "to start getting angry; to flare up",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to start getting angry; to flare up; to lose one's temper",
      "explanation": "To suddenly begin to get angry. The {出|だ}す component stresses the abrupt onset — the anger flares up, often set off by something. A compound of {怒|おこ}る (to get angry) and {出|だ}す."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29598_okoridasu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{父|ちち}が{急|きゅう}に{怒|おこ}り{出|だ}した。",
      "english": "My father suddenly flared up.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29598_okoridasu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}は{小|ちい}さなことで{怒|おこ}り{出|だ}す。",
      "english": "He flies into a rage over little things.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29598_okoridasu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{注意|ちゅうい}されたのが{気|き}に{入|い}らなかったのか、{彼|かれ}は{突然|とつぜん}{怒|おこ}り{出|だ}した。",
      "english": "Apparently he didn't like being warned, because he suddenly flew into a rage.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: Intransitive. Compound verb: {怒|おこ}る + {出|だ}す.\n\nNUANCE: The {出|だ}す component emphasizes the sudden onset of anger — the person abruptly starts getting angry, usually in reaction to something.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {急|きゅう}に{怒|おこ}り{出|だ}す: to suddenly start getting angry\n- {突然|とつぜん}{怒|おこ}り{出|だ}す: to flare up all of a sudden\n\nRELATED:\n- {泣|な}き{出|だ}す: to start crying\n- {笑|わら}い{出|だ}す: to start laughing",
